(RESEARCH DIRECTION FOR THE LAB) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I am interested in treating my own long-running rock practice as a tradition that can be) Tj
T*
(examined, dismantled and resynthesised.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I began making original music in the early 1990s. Instead of presenting that history as) Tj
T*
(nostalgia, I want to ask what happens when its familiar elements - melodic hooks, guitar) Tj
T*
(architecture, vocal phrasing, dramatic structure, studio polish - are pushed toward) Tj
T*
(extremity and then rebuilt.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The next phase I want to explore is a process-based work using:) Tj
T*
(- archival demos and alternate takes;) Tj
T*
(- voice before and after production;) Tj
T*
(- guitar and keyboard material reduced to fragments;) Tj
T*
(- industrial and non-musical textures;) Tj
T*
(- repetition, erosion, stretching and filtering;) Tj
T*
(- live voice against transformed remnants of earlier material.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The difficulty I am currently trying to solve is how to keep the emotional identity of the) Tj
T*
(source while allowing the material to become genuinely unstable and unfamiliar.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The CTM lab would be useful because I want critical feedback on where this approach becomes) Tj
T*
(meaningful research rather than simply a stylistic remix. I also want to learn from artists) Tj
T*
(working with tradition from very different positions, and to test a short solo presentation) Tj
T*
(that makes the transformation process audible.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(PRACTICAL FORMAT) Tj
T*
(Solo artist.) Tj
T*
(Live voice + prepared and transformed audio.) Tj
T*
(Compact technical footprint.) Tj
T*
(15-20 minute presentation can be prepared for the lab.) Tj
